{"type": "reveal", "fact_id": "PF3", "text": "I completed a privacy review thirty minutes ago and confirmed that activity payloads include precise location data. This means events must be tokenized before entering the bus and stored in the EU region, not the default US region as the RFC proposes. I haven't filed the review record yet, but this is a hard requirement -- the combination of precise location data and US-region storage would violate our privacy commitments. Tokenization needs to happen upstream of publishing, which also interacts with Maya's finding about the Avro compatibility gateway and Jon's retention timeline."}
